    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/tektoncd/pipeline/commit/48e9519fc984017b8fd3be3b28309200d494b8bb"/>
    <title>
        test: cover SPIRE client and signing failures
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-18T21:25:36Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11972233?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>waveywaves</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/waveywaves</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;test: cover SPIRE client and signing failures

Exercise missing and invalid configuration, closing an unused client and
request cancellation. Use valid Ed25519 workload identities to verify
that result and manifest signing errors propagate without partial output.

Keep production code and existing tests unchanged.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/01e73cedc42380a198a92419349ecc046a6f8483</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/tektoncd/pipeline/commit/01e73cedc42380a198a92419349ecc046a6f8483"/>
    <title>
        refactor: isolate SPIRE entrypoint runtime dependencies
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-18T21:25:36Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11972233?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>waveywaves</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/waveywaves</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor: isolate SPIRE entrypoint runtime dependencies

Move workload identity acquisition and result signing into internal/spire
so entrypoint does not import controller provisioning dependencies.
Preserve the public SPIRE client interfaces, controller setup, canonical
result format, signing behavior and disable_spire builds.

Keep canonical result/signing helpers shared and add result fixtures and
a configured entrypoint signing/verification round-trip.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
